==================================================
17. PREMIUM ANIMATION SYSTEM
==================================================

Use GSAP and ScrollTrigger where they genuinely add value.

A. Initial page entrance
- Refined hero content reveal.
- Image reveals with carefully controlled motion.
- Staggered appearance for major elements.
- Keep the total entrance quick and unobtrusive.

B. Scroll reveals
- Fade-up or subtle clip-path reveal for selected sections.
- Staggered product card entrances.
- Category image reveals.
- Editorial text and imagery transitions.
- Trigger animations only when content approaches the viewport.

C. Navigation interactions
- Smooth mobile navigation drawer.
- Elegant menu icon state changes.
- Refined header background and spacing transition during scroll.
- Visual feedback on interactive icons.

D. Product cards
- Gentle image zoom on hover.
- Optional alternate image on hover when a real secondary image is available.
- Animated wishlist toggle.
- Subtle Add to Bag feedback.
- No layout shifts.

E. Product detail
- Smooth gallery thumbnail changes.
- Subtle image reveal.
- Animated size selection state.
- Clear cart-added toast transition.
- Smooth related-product entrance.

F. Cart and wishlist
- Smooth cart drawer open and close.
- Staggered cart row entrance where useful.
- Subtle cart count update.
- Clear confirmation after adding or removing an item.

G. Page transitions
- Use the View Transitions API only if suitable and support it with a normal navigation fallback.
- Alternatively implement short page entrance animations.
- Navigation must remain reliable when JavaScript animations fail.

Important animation constraints:
- Keep interactions responsive.
- Never block a user behind a prolonged intro.
- Avoid fake scroll hijacking and unnecessary cursor effects.
- Avoid a huge parallax effect on small screens.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- Ensure all navigation remains usable without animations.
- Prevent layout shifts and horizontal overflow.
- Clean up GSAP ScrollTrigger instances or listeners when necessary.

